# rule name-collision: Cap'n Proto names drop underscores and join other
# words in camel case (#89), so two of the author's names in one struct can
# map to one capnp name. The compiler reports each collision rather than
# inventing a name: two fields (a_b, ab), two enum values ("x_y", "xy"), and
# a field whose nested type's name another field's derives (kindKA beside
# kind with an alternative tagged k: "a", whose struct is KindKA).
# Alternatives are in rule-name-collision-alternatives.
# A label whose name is the reserved extras, the field every struct holds for
# undeclared data, is reported too (extras, and in.Ex_tras, which sanitizes
# to extras): renaming it would leave a reader no way to tell it is the
# author's.
-- in.cue --
import "github.com/sdboyer/thema"

thema.Lineage
name: "collide_names"
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {
	a_b:    string
	ab:     string
	values: "x_y" | "xy"
	kind: {k: "a", n: int8} | {k: "b", s: string}
	kindKA: {x: string}
	extras: string
	in: {Ex_tras: string}
}
lenses: {}
-- out/capnp --
rejected
schema 0.0: ab collides: the label "a_b" and the label "ab" are both named ab in Cap'n Proto, which drops underscores and joins words in camel case; the names in one struct must differ (rule name-collision) @ /in.cue:7:2
schema 0.0: extras collides: the label "extras" is named extras in Cap'n Proto, the name of the field every struct reserves for undeclared data (rule name-collision) @ /in.cue:11:2
schema 0.0: in.Ex_tras collides: the label "Ex_tras" is named extras in Cap'n Proto, the name of the field every struct reserves for undeclared data (rule name-collision) @ /in.cue:12:7
schema 0.0: kindKA collides: the type of kind and the type of kindKA are both named KindKA in Cap'n Proto, which drops underscores and joins words in camel case; the names in one struct must differ (rule name-collision) @ /in.cue:10:2
schema 0.0: values collides: the value "x_y" and the value "xy" are both named xy in Cap'n Proto, which drops underscores and joins words in camel case; the names in one struct must differ (rule name-collision) @ /in.cue:8:2
